      {
        "id": "p36-q13-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "How many have the vowels and consonants alternating?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$144$",
          "worked": "There are 3 vowels and 4 consonants, so the only pattern is CVCVCVC.\n$$4!\\times3!=144$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p36-q13-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "How many have the C immediately following the D?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$720$",
          "worked": "Treat DC as a single unit. There are 6 units to arrange, with the order within DC fixed.\n$$6!=720$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p36-q13-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "How many have the letters N and D separated by exactly 1 letter?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1200$",
          "worked": "Treat N, the intervening letter and D as a single unit. The word then has 5 units.\n\nThere are 2 orders for N and D, 5 choices for the intervening letter and $5!$ arrangements of the units.\n$$2\\times5\\times5!=1200$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 29
      },
      {
        "id": "p36-q13-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "How many have the letters N and D separated by exactly two letters?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$960$",
          "worked": "Treat N, the two intervening letters and D as a single unit. The word then has 4 units.\n\nThere are 2 orders for N and D, ${}^{5}P_{2}$ ordered selections of the intervening letters and $4!$ arrangements of the units.\n$$2\\times{}^{5}P_{2}\\times4!=960$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 29
      },
      {
        "id": "p36-q13-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "How many have the letters N and D separated by more than two letters?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1440$",
          "worked": "Subtract the arrangements in which N and D are adjacent, separated by 1 letter or separated by 2 letters from the total.\n\nFor adjacent N and D, treat them as one unit. Arrange the 6 units and the 2 letters within the unit:\n$$6!\\times2=1440.$$\nUsing parts (f) and (g), the required number is\n$$5040-1440-1200-960=1440.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 33
      }
